# Loan Approval Limits with Arcade.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `bun run dev` boots with every value below blank: GET /health answers
# `"status": "degraded"` and names each capability that is missing, and the
# home page says the same. Fill the REQUIRED block, run
# `bun run setup-arcade <APP_PUBLIC_HOST>`, and restart `bun run dev`.
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit it.

# --- Required: you fill these ------------------------------------------------

# console.anthropic.com → Settings → API keys. The agent's model.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Arcade dashboard → your project → API keys. A project key: setup-arcade
# registers everything in the project it belongs to.
ARCADE_API_KEY=
# Your ngrok static domain, host form, no scheme: `my-app.ngrok.app`. Arcade
# calls the hooks, the loan API and the sign-in endpoints on it, and the
# browser must open the app there too: the sessions and the Arcade verifier
# live on this host only. Blank, the app runs on localhost with sign-in and
# Arcade off.
APP_PUBLIC_HOST=
# The four personas' real addresses. Each is a user of the app's own sign-in,
# and the email is what joins Arcade's user id, the OAuth subject and the loan
# book's actor. Set them before the first boot: the identity and policy
# databases are seeded once. Blank, they seed the @bank.example placeholders.
PERSONA_LOAN_OFFICER_EMAIL=
PERSONA_CREDIT_ANALYST_EMAIL=
PERSONA_VP_CREDIT_EMAIL=
PERSONA_CHIEF_CREDIT_OFFICER_EMAIL=

# --- Filled in by `bun run setup-arcade <APP_PUBLIC_HOST>`: leave blank ------
# It writes a value only where this file has none, and never overwrites one.

# Seals the per-browser session cookie (AES-256-GCM). At least 32 characters.
SESSION_SECRET=
# Signs identity sessions and encrypts the ID-token signing key in idp.db.
# Blank is a published development secret, which the app accepts only on
# localhost: with APP_PUBLIC_HOST set to anything else, sign-in is refused and
# /health says why. Changing it makes idp.db's signing key unreadable; the app
# then refuses to start identity and names the fix (delete the local idp.db).
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# The app's own sign-in client at its identity provider.
IDP_CLIENT_ID=
IDP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The OAuth clients the identity provider keeps: `arcade` (Arcade's hop-2
# provider), `arcade-user-source` (hop 1) and `web` (the app's sign-in), each
# with the redirect URIs it allowlists.
IDP_OAUTH_CLIENTS=
IDP_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS_ARCADE=
IDP_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS_ARCADE_USER_SOURCE=
IDP_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS_WEB=
# The bearer Arcade presents on every /hooks call. Registered with the hooks.
ARCADE_HOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=
# The bearer the approvals toolkit presents to the app. Also an Arcade tool secret.
APPROVALS_STORE_TOKEN=
# The gateway's slug. setup-arcade creates the gateway under it.
ARCADE_GATEWAY_ID=
# `hooks`: the panel at /panel watches the live control plane. Blank, it
# replays a fixture under `next dev`, and says so on screen.
GOVERNANCE_STREAM=

# --- Optional: the defaults are right; uncomment to change -------------------

# The model id.
# MODEL_ID=claude-sonnet-5
# The app's port. Mastra Studio (`bun run studio`) takes STUDIO_PORT.
# PORT=3000
# STUDIO_PORT=4111
# The bearer for POST /hooks/admin/reset, /bank/admin/reset and
# /identity/admin/reset, and `bun run reset`. Blank, those routes do not exist.
# RESET_TOKEN=
# `off` strips act 4's free-text injection scanners, to show what they
# prevent. Blank is armed.
# INJECTION_DETECTION=
# Toolkit names as Arcade files them.
# ARCADE_LOAN_TOOLKIT=Loan
# ARCADE_APPROVALS_TOOLKIT=Approvals
# The Arcade org and project setup-arcade registers the hooks and the gateway
# in. Blank, it takes the Arcade CLI's active ones, as `arcade whoami` shows them.
# ARCADE_ORG_ID=
# ARCADE_PROJECT_ID=
# The User Source's id (us_...), which the gateway authenticates through. Or
# pass it once as `bun run setup-arcade <host> --user-source <id>`.
# ARCADE_USER_SOURCE_ID=
# Where tools and the gateway are, and where the verifier confirms users.
# ARCADE_API_URL=https://api.arcade.dev
# ARCADE_CLOUD_URL=https://cloud.arcade.dev
# Pins the MCP client id hop 1 authorizes under, so a restart does not cost
# every persona another Arcade consent screen. Blank registers one per process.
# ARCADE_MCP_CLIENT_ID=
# What the app's sign-in asks for. `email` is required.
# IDP_SCOPES=openid email
# The redirect URIs for any client without its own IDP_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS_<KEY>.
# IDP_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS=https://cloud.arcade.dev/api/v1/oauth/callback
# The three SQLite files, seeded from fixtures when empty.
# GOVERNANCE_DB_PATH=./governance.db
# LOANS_DB_PATH=./loans.db
# IDP_DB_PATH=./idp.db
# The control plane's own deadline per hook (ms), how often it re-reads the
# policy (ms), and how long an approval's grant lasts (s).
# HOOK_DEADLINE_MS=2500
# POLICY_POLL_MS=250
# GRANT_TTL_SECONDS=900
# Where the app's server-side code reads its own control plane and identity
# provider. Blank is localhost:$PORT, never the public host.
# CONTROL_PLANE_HOST=
# IDENTITY_HOST=
